  "result": "Fixed in `src/click/types.py`. `IntRange._clamp` moved the wrong way when a bound was open. It returned `bound - dir`, which pushed the value outside the allowed range. For example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`. It now returns `bound + dir`.\n\nI checked the two open-bound cases directly. With `min_open=True`, `-5` now clamps to `1`. With `max_open=True`, `50` now clamps to `9`. `tests/test_types.py` passes (41 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't add a regression test, and the existing tests only cover closed bounds.",
